#. type: Title #
#: en/./developers/opml.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "OPML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS supports the [OPML](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OPML) format to "
"export and import lists of RSS/Atom feeds in a standard way, compatible with "
"several other RSS aggregators."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"However, FreshRSS also supports several additional features not covered by "
"the basic OPML specification.  Luckily, the [OPML "
"specification](http://opml.org/spec2.opml) allows extensions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> *An OPML file may contain elements and attributes not described on this "
"page, only if those elements are defined in a namespace.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "and:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> *OPML can also be extended by the addition of new values for the type "
"attribute.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./developers/opml.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "FreshRSS OPML extension"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS uses the XML namespace <https://freshrss.org/opml> to export/import "
"extended information not covered by the basic OPML specification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The list of the custom FreshRSS attributes can be seen in [the source "
"code](https://github.com/FreshRSS/FreshRSS/blob/edge/app/views/helpers/export/opml.phtml), "
"and here is an overview:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTML+XPath or XML+XPath"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<outline type=\"HTML+XPath\" ...`: Additional type of source, which is not "
"RSS/Atom, but HTML Web Scraping using "
"[XPath](https://www.w3.org/TR/xpath-10/) 1.0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ [XPath 1.0](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XPath) is a standard query "
"language, which FreshRSS supports to enable [Web "
"scraping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_scraping).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<outline type=\"XML+XPath\" ...`: Same than `HTML+XPath` but using an XML "
"parser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The following attributes are using similar naming conventions than "
"[RSS-Bridge](https://rss-bridge.github.io/rss-bridge/Bridge_API/XPathAbstract.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItem`: XPath expression for extracting the feed items from the "
"source page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `//div[@class=\"news-item\"]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemTitle`: XPath expression for extracting the item’s title from "
"the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `descendant::h2`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemContent`: XPath expression for extracting an item’s content "
"from the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `.`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemUri`: XPath expression for extracting an item link from the "
"item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `descendant::a/@href`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemAuthor`: XPath expression for extracting an item author from "
"the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `\"Anonymous\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemTimestamp`: XPath expression for extracting an item timestamp "
"from the item context. The result will be parsed by "
"[`strtotime()`](https://php.net/strtotime)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemTimeFormat`: Date/Time format to parse the timestamp, "
"according to "
"[`DateTime::createFromFormat()`](https://php.net/datetime.createfromformat)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemThumbnail`: XPath expression for extracting an item’s "
"thumbnail (image) URL from the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `descendant::img/@src`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemCategories`: XPath expression for extracting a list of "
"categories (tags) from the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:xPathItemUid`: XPath expression for extracting an item’s unique ID "
"from the item context. If left empty, a hash is computed automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "JSON+DotNotation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<outline type=\"JSON+DotNotation\" ...`: Similar to `HTML+XPath` but for "
"JSON and using a dot/bracket syntax such as "
"`object.object.array[2].property`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItem`: JSON dot notation for extracting the feed items from the "
"source page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `data.items`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemTitle`: JSON dot notation for extracting the item’s title from "
"the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `meta.title`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemContent`: JSON dot notation for extracting an item’s content "
"from the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `content`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemUri`: JSON dot notation for extracting an item link from the "
"item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `meta.links[0]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemAuthor`: JSON dot notation for extracting an item author from "
"the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemTimestamp`: JSON dot notation for extracting an item timestamp "
"from the item context. The result will be parsed by "
"[`strtotime()`](https://php.net/strtotime)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemTimeFormat`: Date/Time format to parse the timestamp, "
"according to "
"[`DateTime::createFromFormat()`](https://php.net/datetime.createfromformat)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemThumbnail`: JSON dot notation for extracting an item’s "
"thumbnail (image) URL from the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemCategories`: JSON dot notation for extracting a list of "
"categories (tags) from the item context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:jsonItemUid`: JSON dot notation for extracting an item’s unique ID "
"from the item context. If left empty, a hash is computed automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "JSON Feed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<outline type=\"JSONFeed\" ...`: Uses `JSON+DotNotation` behind the scenes "
"to parse a [JSON Feed](https://www.jsonfeed.org/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTML+XPath+JSON"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<outline type=\"HTML+XPath+JSON+DotNotation\" frss:xPathToJson=\"...\" "
"...`: Same as `JSON+DotNotation` but first extracting the JSON string from "
"an HTML document thanks to an XPath expression."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `//script[@type='application/json']`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:81
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "cURL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A number of [cURL options](https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_easy_setopt.html) "
"are supported:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_COOKIE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_COOKIEFILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_MAXREDIRS`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_POST`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_PROXY`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_PROXYTYPE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "`frss:CURLOPT_USERAGENT`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:priority`: Used for priority / visibility of the articles of that "
"feed. Can be: `important`, `main` (default), `category`, `feed`, `hidden`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:unicityCriteria`: Criteria used for the unicity of articles. E.g. `id` "
"(default), `link`, `sha1:link_published`, `sha1:link_published_title`, "
"`sha1:title`, "
"[etc](https://github.com/FreshRSS/FreshRSS/blob/1c92d55917029d291d00009b674d8552934a69ec/app/Models/Feed.php#L652-L666)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:unicityCriteriaForced`: Boolean to force the usage of the selected "
"unicity criterion even in the case of many duplicates (otherwise, the "
"default behaviour is to fall back to a more precise unicity criteria)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:cssFullContent`: [CSS "
"Selector](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Selectors) to "
"enable the download and extraction of the matching HTML section of each "
"articles’ Web address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Example: `div.main, .summary`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:cssContentFilter`: [CSS "
"Selector](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Selectors) to "
"remove the matching HTML elements from the article content or from the full "
"content retrieved by `frss:cssFullContent`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/opml.md:107
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t* Example: `.footer, .aside`\n"
". `frss:cssFullContentConditions`: List (separated by a new line) of search "
"queries to trigger a full content retrieval as defined by "
"`frss:cssFullContent`.\n"
"* `frss:filtersActionRead`: List (separated by a new line) of search queries "
"to automatically mark a new article as read.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic OPML (reading lists)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/opml.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`frss:opmlUrl`: If non-empty, indicates that this outline (category) should "
"be dynamically populated from a remote OPML at the specified URL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/opml.md:112
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (xml)
#: en/./developers/opml.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"<opml version=\"2.0\">\n"
"\t<head>\n"
"\t\t<title>FreshRSS OPML extension example</title>\n"
"\t</head>\n"
"\t<body>\n"
"\t\t<outline xmlns:frss=\"https://freshrss.org/opml\"\n"
"\t\t\ttext=\"Example\"\n"
"\t\t\ttype=\"HTML+XPath\"\n"
"\t\t\txmlUrl=\"https://www.example.net/page.html\"\n"
"\t\t\thtmlUrl=\"https://www.example.net/page.html\"\n"
"\t\t\tdescription=\"Example of Web scraping\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:priority=\"main\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:xPathItem=\"//a[contains(@href, "
"'/interesting/')]/ancestor::article\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:xPathItemTitle=\"descendant::h2\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:xPathItemContent=\".\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:xPathItemUri=\"descendant::a[string-length(@href)&gt;0]/@href\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:xPathItemThumbnail=\"descendant::img/@src\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:cssFullContent=\"article\"\n"
"\t\t\tfrss:filtersActionRead=\"intitle:⚡️ OR intitle:🔥&#10;something\"\n"
"\t\t/>\n"
"\t</body>\n"
"</opml>\n"
msgstr ""

