#. type: Title ##
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "About FreshRSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS is an RSS / Atom feed aggregator written in PHP dating back to "
"October 2012. The official site is located at "
"[freshrss.org](https://freshrss.org) and the official repository is hosted "
"on GitHub: "
"[github.com/FreshRSS/FreshRSS](https://github.com/FreshRSS/FreshRSS)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The problem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "FreshRSS is limited in its technical possibilities by various factors:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "The number of developers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "The will to integrate certain changes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "The level of \"hacking\" required to integrate marginal features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"While the first limitation can, in theory, be lifted by the participation of "
"new contributors to the project, it depends on the willingness of "
"contributors to take an interest in the source code of the entire "
"project. In order to remove the other two limitations, most of the time it "
"will be necessary to create a \"fork\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Another solution consists of an extension system. By allowing users to write "
"their own extension without taking an interest in the core of the basic "
"software, we allow for:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Reducing the amount of source code a new contributor has to take in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Unofficial integration of novelties"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "No forking or main developer approval required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Note: it is quite conceivable that the functionalities of an extension can "
"later be officially integrated into the FreshRSS code. Extensions make it "
"easy to propose a proof of concept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Minz Framework"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "see [Minz documentation](minz.md)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Write an extension for FreshRSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Here we are! We’ve talked about the most useful features of Minz and how to "
"run FreshRSS correctly and it’s about time to address the extensions "
"themselves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"An extension allows you to easily add functionality to FreshRSS without "
"having to touch the core of the project directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Make it work in Docker"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When working on an extension, it’s easier to see it working directly in its "
"environment. With Docker, you can leverage the use of the ```volume``` "
"option when starting the container. Hopefully, you can use it without "
"Docker-related knowledge by using the Makefile rule:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"make start extensions=\"/full/path/to/extension/1 "
"/full/path/to/extension/2\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Basic files and folders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The first thing to note is that **all** extensions **must** be located in "
"the `extensions` directory, at the base of the FreshRSS tree.  An extension "
"is a directory containing a set of mandatory (and optional) files and "
"subdirectories.  The convention requires that the main directory name be "
"preceded by an \"x\" to indicate that it is not an extension included by "
"default in FreshRSS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The main directory of an extension must contain at least two **mandatory** "
"files:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A `metadata.json` file that contains a description of the extension. This "
"file is written in JSON."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"An `extension.php` file containing the entry point of the extension (which "
"is a class that inherits Minz_Extension)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please note that there is a not a required link between the directory name "
"of the extension and the name of the class inside `extension.php`, but you "
"should follow our best practice: If you want to write a `HelloWorld` "
"extension, the directory name should be `xExtension-HelloWorld` and the base "
"class name `HelloWorldExtension`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the file `freshrss/extensions/xExtension-HelloWorld/extension.php` you "
"need the structure:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"final class HelloWorldExtension extends Minz_Extension {\n"
"\t#[\\Override]\n"
"\tpublic function init(): void {\n"
"\t\tparent::init();\n"
"\n"
"\t\t// your code here\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There is an example HelloWorld extension that you can download from [our "
"GitHub repo](https://github.com/FreshRSS/xExtension-HelloWorld)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You may also need additional files or subdirectories depending on your "
"needs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`configure.phtml` is the file containing the form to parameterize your "
"extension"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A `static/` directory containing CSS and JavaScript files that you will need "
"for your extension (note that if you need to write a lot of CSS it may be "
"more interesting to write a complete theme)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid "A `Controllers` directory containing additional controllers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid "An `i18n` directory containing additional translations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`layout` and `views` directories to define new views or to overwrite the "
"current views"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In addition, it is good to have a `LICENSE` file indicating the license "
"under which your extension is distributed and a `README` file giving a "
"detailed description of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The metadata.json file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The `metadata.json` file defines your extension through a number of "
"important elements. It must contain a valid JSON array containing the "
"following entries:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid "`name`: the name of your extension"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`author`: your name, your e-mail address … but there is no specific format "
"to adopt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid "`description`: a description of your extension"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid "`version`: the current version number of the extension"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:98
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* `entrypoint`: Indicates the entry point of your extension. It must match "
"the name of the class contained in the file `extension.php` without the "
"suffix `Extension`\n"
"(so if the entry point is `HelloWorld`, your class will be called "
"`HelloWorldExtension`)\n"
"* `type`: Defines the type of your extension. There are two types: `system` "
"and `user`. We will study this difference right after.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only the `name` and `entrypoint` fields are required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:101
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing between `system` and `user`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:104
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A *user* extension can be enabled by some users and not by others (typically "
"for user preferences)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid "A *system* extension in comparison is enabled for every account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:107
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Writing your own extension.php"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This file is the core of your extension.  It must define some key elements "
"to be loaded by the extension system:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The class name must be the `entrypoint` value defined in the `metadata.json` "
"file suffixed by `Extension` (if your `entrypoint` value is `HelloWorld`, "
"your class name will be `HelloWorldExtension`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The class must extend the `Minz_Extension` abstract class which defines the "
"core methods and properties of a FreshRSS extension."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The class must define the `init` method. This method is called **only** if "
"the extension is loaded. Its purpose is to initialize the extension and its "
"behavior during every page load."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The `Minz_Extension` abstract class defines a set of methods that can be "
"overridden to fit your needs: * the `install` method is called when the user "
"enables the extension in the configuration page. It must return `true` when "
"successful and a string containing an error message when not. Its purpose is "
"to prepare FreshRSS for the extension (adding a table to the database, "
"creating a folder tree, …).  * the `uninstall` method is called when the "
"user disables the extension in the configuration page. It must return `true` "
"when successful and a string containing an error message when not. Its "
"purpose is to clean FreshRSS (removing a table from the database, deleting a "
"folder tree, …). Usually it reverts changes introduced by the `install` "
"method.  * the `handleConfigureAction` method is called when a user loads "
"the extension configuration panel. It contains the logic to validate and "
"store the submitted values defined in the `configure.phtml` file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:122
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> If your extension code is scattered in different classes, you need to load "
"their source before using them. Of course you could include the files "
"manually, but it’s more efficient to load them automatically. To do so, you "
"just need to define the `autoload` method which will include them when "
"needed. This method will be registered automatically when the extension is "
"enabled.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:138
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Minz_Extension` abstract class defines another set of methods that "
"should not be overridden:\n"
"* the `getName`, `getEntrypoint`, `getPath`, `getAuthor`, `getDescription`, "
"`getVersion`, and `getType` methods return the extension internal "
"properties. Those properties are extracted from the `metadata.json` file.\n"
"* `getFileUrl(string $filename, bool $isStatic = true): string` will return "
"the URL to a file in the `static` directory.\n"
"\tThe first parameter is the name of the file (without `static/`).\n"
"\tSet `$isStatic` to true for user-independent files, and to `false` for "
"files saved in a user’s own directory.\n"
"* the `registerController` method registers an extension controller in "
"FreshRSS. The selected controller must be defined in the extension "
"*Controllers* folder, its file name must be `<name>Controller.php`, and its "
"class name must be `FreshExtension_<name>_Controller`.\n"
"* the `registerViews` method registers the extension views in FreshRSS.\n"
"* the `registerTranslates` method registers the extension translation files "
"in FreshRSS.\n"
"* the `registerHook` method registers hook actions in different part of the "
"application.\n"
"* the `getSystemConfiguration*()` family of methods retrieve typed extension "
"configuration values for the system.\n"
"* the `setSystemConfigurationValue()` method stores an extension "
"configuration value for the system.\n"
"* the `removeSystemConfiguration` method removes the extension configuration "
"for the system.\n"
"* the `getUserConfiguration*()` family of methods retrieve typed extension "
"configuration values for the current user.\n"
"* the `setUserConfigurationValue()` method stores an extension configuration "
"value for the current user.\n"
"* the `removeUserConfiguration` method removes the extension configuration "
"for the current user.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:140
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Note that if you modify the later set of methods, you might break the "
"extension system. Thus making FreshRSS unusable. So it’s highly recommended "
"to let those unmodified.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:141
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The \"hooks\" system"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:147
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can register at the FreshRSS event system in an extensions `init()` "
"method, to manipulate data when some of the core functions are executed.  "
"The last parameter is the priority of the hook when triggered.  The hook "
"with the lowest priority value are triggered first.  The default priority is "
"0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"final class HelloWorldExtension extends Minz_Extension\n"
"{\n"
"\t#[\\Override]\n"
"\tpublic function init(): void {\n"
"\t\tparent::init();\n"
"\n"
"\t\t$this->registerHook(Minz_HookType::EntryBeforeDisplay, [$this, "
"'renderEntry'], 10);\n"
"\t\t$this->registerHook(Minz_HookType::CheckUrlBeforeAdd, [self::class, "
"'checkUrl'], -10);\n"
"\t}\n"
"\n"
"\tpublic function renderEntry(FreshRSS_Entry $entry): FreshRSS_Entry {\n"
"\t\t$message = $this->getUserConfigurationString('message');\n"
"\t\t$entry->_content(\"<h1>{$message}</h1>\" . $entry->content());\n"
"\t\treturn $entry;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\n"
"\tpublic static function checkUrlBeforeAdd(string $url): string {\n"
"\t\tif (str_starts_with($url, 'https://')) {\n"
"\t\t\treturn $url;\n"
"\t\t}\n"
"\t\treturn null;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:175
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:230
#, markdown-text
msgid "The following events are available:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:184
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* `Minz_HookType::ActionExecute` (`function(Minz_ActionController "
"$controller): bool`): Called before an action is executed in "
"`Minz_Dispatcher::launchAction()`.\n"
"\tBy returning `true`, you allow the original action to proceed further; "
"`false` stops further execution of the action.\n"
"\tThis hook can be used for adding extra functionality to an existing "
"action. See also: `Minz_Request::is()`, `Minz_Request::controllerName()`, "
"`Minz_Request::actionName()`.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::ApiMisc` (`function(): void`): to allow extensions to have "
"their own API endpoint\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::BeforeLoginBtn` (`function(): string`): Allows to insert "
"HTML before the login button. Applies to the create button on the register "
"page as well. Example use case is inserting a captcha widget.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::CheckUrlBeforeAdd` (`function($url) -> Url | null`): will "
"be executed every time a URL is added. The URL itself will be passed as "
"parameter. This way a website known to have feeds which doesn’t advertise it "
"in the header can still be automatically supported.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::CustomFaviconBtnUrl` (`function(FreshRSS_Feed $feed): "
"string | null`): Allows extensions to implement a button for setting a "
"custom favicon for individual feeds by providing an URL. The URL will be "
"sent a POST request with the `extAction` field set to either "
"`query_icon_info` or `update_icon`, along with an `id` field which describes "
"the feed's ID.\n"
"Example response for a `query_icon_info` request:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\"extName\":\"YouTube Video Feed\",\"iconUrl\":\"..\\/f.php?h=40838a43\"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:212
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`Minz_HookType::CustomFaviconHash` (`function(FreshRSS_Feed $feed): string | "
"null`): Enables the modification of custom favicon hashes by returning "
"params from the hook function. The hook should check if the "
"`customFaviconExt` attribute of `$feed` is set to the extension's name "
"before returning a custom value. Otherwise, the return value should be null."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:212
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* `Minz_HookType::EntriesFavorite` (`function(array $ids, bool "
"$is_favorite): void`):\n"
"\twill be executed when some entries are marked or unmarked as favorites "
"(starred)\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::EntryAutoRead` (`function(FreshRSS_Entry $entry, string "
"$why): void`): Triggered when an entry is automatically marked as read. The "
"*why* parameter supports the rules {`filter`, `upon_reception`, "
"`same_title_in_feed`, `same_guid_in_category`}.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::EntryAutoUnread` (`function(FreshRSS_Entry $entry, string "
"$why): void`): Triggered when an entry is automatically marked as "
"unread. The *why* parameter supports the rules {`updated_article`}.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::EntryBeforeDisplay` (`function($entry) -> Entry | null`): "
"will be executed every time an entry is rendered. The entry itself (instance "
"of FreshRSS\\_Entry) will be passed as parameter.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::EntryBeforeInsert` (`function($entry) -> Entry | null`): "
"will be executed when a feed is refreshed and new entries will be imported "
"into the database. The new entry (instance of FreshRSS\\_Entry) will be "
"passed as parameter.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::EntryBeforeAdd` (`function($entry) -> Entry | null`): will "
"be executed when a feed is refreshed and just before an entry is added to "
"the database. Useful for reading the final state of the entry after filter "
"actions have been applied. The new entry (instance of FreshRSS\\_Entry) will "
"be passed as parameter.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::EntryBeforeUpdate` (`function($entry) -> Entry | null`): "
"will be executed when a feed is refreshed and just before an entry is "
"updated in the database. Useful for reading the final state of the entry "
"after filter actions have been applied. The updated entry (instance of "
"FreshRSS\\_Entry) will be passed as parameter.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::FeedBeforeActualize` (`function($feed) -> Feed | null`): "
"will be executed when a feed is updated. The feed (instance of "
"FreshRSS\\_Feed) will be passed as parameter.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::FeedBeforeInsert` (`function($feed) -> Feed | null`): will "
"be executed when a new feed is imported into the database. The new feed "
"(instance of FreshRSS\\_Feed) will be passed as parameter.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::FeedsListBeforeActualize` (`function(array<FreshRSS_Feed> "
"$feedList) -> array | null`): will be executed before FreshRSS tries to "
"update feeds. The list of feeds (array of `FreshRSS_Feed`) to update will be "
"passed as a parameter. Useful for modifying the order in which the feeds "
"will be updated.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::FreshrssInit` (`function() -> none`): will be executed at "
"the end of the initialization of FreshRSS, useful to initialize components "
"or to do additional access checks.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::FreshrssUserMaintenance` (`function() -> none`): will be "
"executed for each user during the `actualize_script`, useful to run some "
"maintenance tasks on the user.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::JsVars` (`function($vars = array) -> array | null`): will "
"be executed if the `jsonVars` in the header will be generated.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::MenuAdminEntry` (`function() -> string`): add an entry at "
"the end of the \"Administration\" menu, the returned string must be valid "
"HTML (e.g. `<li class=\"item active\"><a href=\"url\">New "
"entry</a></li>`).\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::MenuConfigurationEntry` (`function() -> string`): add an "
"entry at the end of the \"Configuration\" menu, the returned string must be "
"valid HTML (e.g. `<li class=\"item active\"><a href=\"url\">New "
"entry</a></li>`).\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::MenuOtherEntry` (`function() -> string`): add an entry at "
"the end of the header dropdown menu (i.e. after the \"About\" entry), the "
"returned string must be valid HTML (e.g. `<li class=\"item active\"><a "
"href=\"url\">New entry</a></li>`).\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::NavEntries` (`function() -> string`): will add DOM "
"elements before the navigation buttons.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::NavMenu` (`function() -> string`): will be executed if the "
"navigation was built.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::NavReadingModes` (`function($reading_modes) -> array | "
"null`): **TODO** add documentation.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::PostUpdate` (`function(none) -> none`): **TODO** add "
"documentation.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::SimplepieAfterInit` (`function(FreshRSS_SimplePieCustom "
"$simplePie, FreshRSS_Feed $feed, bool $result): void`): Triggered after "
"fetching an RSS/Atom feed with SimplePie. Useful for instance to get the "
"HTTP response headers (e.g. `$simplePie->data['headers']`).\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::SimplepieBeforeInit` (`function(FreshRSS_SimplePieCustom "
"$simplePie, FreshRSS_Feed $feed): void`): Triggered before fetching an "
"RSS/Atom feed with SimplePie.\n"
"* `Minz_HookType::ViewModes` (`function(array<FreshRSS_ViewMode> "
"$viewModes): array|null`): Allow extensions to register additional view "
"modes than *normal*, *reader*, *global*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./developers/writing-extensions.md:214
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ Note: the `Minz_HookType::Simplepie*` hooks are only fired for feeds "
"using SimplePie via pull, i.e. normal RSS/Atom feeds. This excludes WebSub "
"(push), and the various HTML or JSON Web scraping methods.\n"
msgstr ""

