#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "By content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is possible to filter articles by their content by inputting a string in "
"the search field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "With the search field"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can use the search field to further refine results:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by feed ID: `f:123` or multiple feed IDs (*or*): `f:123,234,345`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by category ID: `c:23` or multiple category IDs (*or*): `c:23,34,45`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by author: `author:name` or `author:'composed name'`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by title: `intitle:keyword` or `intitle:'composed keyword'`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by text (content): `intext:keyword` or `intext:'composed keyword'`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by URL: `inurl:keyword` or `inurl:'composed keyword'`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by tag: `#tag` or `#tag+with+whitespace` or `#'tag with whitespace'`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by free-text: `keyword` or `'composed keyword'`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by date of discovery, using the [ISO 8601 time interval "
"format](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601#Time_intervals): "
"`date:<date-interval>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "From a specific day, or month, or year:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-03-30`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-03` or `date:201403`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "From a specific time of a given day:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-05-30T13`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-05-30T13:30`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Between two given dates:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-02/2014-04`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-02--2014-04`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-02/04`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-02-03/05`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-02-03T22:00/22:15`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-02-03T22:00/15`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "After a given date:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-03/`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Before a given date:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:/2014-03`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a specific duration after a given date:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:2014-03/P1W`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a specific duration before a given date:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P1W/2014-05-25T23:59:59`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "For the past duration before now (the trailing slash is optional):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P1Y/` or `date:P1Y` (past year)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P2M/` (past two months)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P3W/` (past three weeks)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P4D/` (past four days)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:PT5H/` (past five hours)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:PT30M/` (past thirty minutes)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:PT90S/` (past ninety seconds)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P1DT1H/` (past one day and one hour)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "From the oldest until some time before now:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`!date:P1M` (older than one month before now, using a negation)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '			* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Note: the syntax ~~`date:/P1M`~~ is not supported"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Date constraints may be combined:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '		* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "`date:P1Y !date:P1M` (from one year before now until one month before now)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "by date of publication, using the same format: `pubdate:<date-interval>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by date of server modification, using the same format: "
"`mdate:<date-interval>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by date of user modification (e.g. mark as read or favourite), using the "
"same format: `userdate:<date-interval>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by custom label ID `L:12` or multiple label IDs: `L:12,13,14` or with any "
"label: `L:*`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by custom label name `label:label`, `label:\"my label\"` or any label name "
"from a list (*or*): `labels:\"my label,my other label\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by several label names (*and*): `label:\"my label\" label:\"my other "
"label\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by entry (article) ID: `e:1639310674957894` or multiple entry IDs (*or*): "
"`e:1639310674957894,1639310674957893`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"by user query (saved search) name: `search:myQuery`, `search:\"My query\"` "
"or saved search ID: `S:3` or multiple search IDs: `S:1,2`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"internally, those references are replaced by the corresponding user query in "
"the search expression"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:109
#, markdown-text
msgid "Be careful not to enter a space between the operator and the search value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Some operators can be used negatively, to exclude articles, with the same "
"syntax as above, but prefixed by a `!` or `-`: `!f:234`, `-author:name`, "
"`-intitle:keyword`, `-inurl:keyword`, `-#tag`, `!keyword`, `!date:2019`, "
"`!date:P1W`, `!pubdate:P3d/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is also possible to combine keywords to create a more precise filter.  "
"For example, you can enter multiple instances of `f:`, `author:`, "
"`intitle:`, `intext:`, `inurl:`, `#`, and free-text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:118
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Combining several search criteria implies a logical *and*, but the keyword ` "
"OR ` can be used to combine several search criteria with a logical *or* "
"instead: `author:Dupont OR author:Dupond`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:121
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You don’t have to do anything special to combine multiple negative "
"operators. Writing `!intitle:'thing1' !intitle:'thing2'` implies AND, see "
"above. For more pointers on how AND and OR interact with negation, see [this "
"GitHub "
"comment](https://github.com/FreshRSS/FreshRSS/issues/3236#issuecomment-891219460).  "
"Additional reading: [De Morgan’s "
"laws](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Morgan%27s_laws)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ Searches are applied to the HTML content, and special XML characters "
"`<&\">` are automatically encoded (so one can search for `'A & B'` without "
"having to encode the `&amp;`).\n"
"> To search HTML tags, one must use regex searches (see below).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:126
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Finally, parentheses may be used to express more complex queries, with basic "
"negation support:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:132
#, markdown-text
msgid "`(author:Alice OR intitle:hello) (author:Bob OR intitle:world)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:132
#, markdown-text
msgid "`(author:Alice intitle:hello) OR (author:Bob intitle:world)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:132
#, markdown-text
msgid "`!((author:Alice intitle:hello) OR (author:Bob intitle:world))`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:132
#, markdown-text
msgid "`(author:Alice intitle:hello) !(author:Bob intitle:world)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:132
#, markdown-text
msgid "`!(S:1 OR S:2)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:134
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ If you need to search for a parenthesis, it needs to be escaped like "
"`\\(` or `\\)` or used inside a quoted string like `\"a (b)\"`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Regex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:138
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Text searches (including `author:`, `intitle:`, `inurl:`, `#`) may use "
"regular expressions, which must be enclosed in `/ /`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:140
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Regex searches are case-sensitive by default, but can be made "
"case-insensitive with the `i` modifier like: `/Alice/i`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid "Supports multiline mode with `m` modifier, like: `/^Alice/m`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:146
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ `author:` is working with one author per line, so the multiline mode "
"may advantageously be used, like: `author:/^Alice Dupont$/im`\n"
">\n"
"> ℹ️ `#` is likewise working with one tag per line, so the multiline mode "
"may advantageously be used, like: `#/^Hello World$/im`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:148
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Example to search entries, which title starts with the *Lol* word, with any "
"number of *o*: `intitle:/^Lo+l/i`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:150
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Example to search empty entries (where the body of articles is blank): "
"`intext:/^\\s*$/`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:152
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As opposed to normal searches, special XML characters `<&\">` are not "
"escaped in regex searches, to allow searching HTML code, like: `/Hello "
"<span>world<\\/span>/`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:154
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> ℹ️ A literal slash needs to be escaped, like `\\/`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:156
#, markdown-text
msgid "⚠️ Advanced regex syntax details depend on the regex engine used:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS filter actions such as auto-mark-as-read and auto-favourite use "
"[PHP preg_match](https://php.net/function.preg-match)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid "Regex searches depend on which database you are using:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid "For SQLite, [PHP preg_match](https://php.net/function.preg-match) is used;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[For "
"PostgreSQL](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/functions-matching.html#FUNCTIONS-POSIX-REGEXP);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid "[For MariaDB](https://mariadb.com/kb/en/pcre/);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '	* '
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[For "
"MySQL](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.0/en/regexp.html#function_regexp-like)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:165
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ Even with PostgreSQL, you are welcome to use `\\b` for word boundary "
"(and `\\B` for the opposite), as there is an automatic translation to `\\y` "
"and `\\Y`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:166
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "By sorting by date"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can change the sort order by clicking the toggle button available in the "
"header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:170 en/./users/user-queries.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bookmark the current query"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:173
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Once you came up with your perfect filter, it would be a shame if you had to "
"recreate it every time you need to use it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:177
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Luckily, there is a way to bookmark them for later use.  We call them [*user "
"queries*](./user-queries.md).  You can create as many as you want, the only "
"limit is how they will be displayed on your screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:179
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Read more about [*user queries*](./user-queries.md) to learn how to create "
"them, use them, and even reshare them via HTML / RSS / OPML."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/filtering-articles.md:184
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Read more: * [Normal, Global and Reader view](./views.md)  * [Refreshing the "
"feeds](./refreshing-feeds.md)  * [User queries](./user-queries.md)"
msgstr ""

