msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Manual update"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you can’t or don’t want to use the automatic method, you can update "
"manually. There are two methods for updating all or some of the feeds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Complete update"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This update occurs on all feeds. To trigger it, simply click on the update "
"link in the navigation menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Navigation menu](../img/users/refresh.1.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When the update starts, a progress bar appears and changes while feeds are "
"processed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress bar](../img/users/refresh.5.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Partial update"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This update occurs on the selected feed only. To trigger it, simply click on "
"the update link in the feed menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Feed menu](../img/users/refresh.2.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Automatic update with cron"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "This is the recommended method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This method is only available if you have access to the scheduled tasks of "
"the machine on which your FreshRSS instance is installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The script is named *actualize_script.php* and is located in the *app* "
"folder. The scheduled task syntax will not be explained here. However, here "
"is [a quick introduction to "
"crontab](http://www.adminschoice.com/crontab-quick-reference/) that might "
"help you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "Here is an example to trigger article update every hour."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (cron)
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0 * * * * php /path/to/FreshRSS/app/actualize_script.php > /tmp/FreshRSS.log "
"2>&1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Online cron"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you do not have access to the installation server scheduled task, you can "
"still automate the update process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To do so, you need to create a scheduled task, which need to call a specific "
"URL: <https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize> (it could be "
"different depending on your installation). Depending on your application "
"authentication method, you need to adapt the scheduled task."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid "Special parameters to configure the script - all parameters can be combined:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Parameter `ajax` <https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&ajax=1> "
"Only a status site is returned and not a complete website. Example: \"OK\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Parameter `maxFeeds` "
"<https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&maxFeeds=30> If "
"*maxFeeds* is set the configured amount of feeds is refreshed at once. The "
"default setting is `10`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Parameters `user` and `token` "
"<https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&user=alice&token=token123> "
"Security parameters that allow a user to refresh their feed when *Web form* "
"authentication is set. For detailed Documentation see “Form authentication” "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For Form Authentication (Web form)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your FreshRSS instance is using Form Authentication, you can configure a "
"*Master authentication token* in a user profile to grant access to the "
"online cron."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Token configuration](../img/users/token.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After setting the authentication token, use the `user` and `token` "
"parameters to call the online cron script. For the above example, the syntax "
"for the scheduled task will look as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:88
#, markdown-text
msgid "<https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&maxFeeds=10&ajax=1&user=alice&token=token123>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Alternatively, but not recommended, you can also allow anonymous users to "
"update feeds (*Allow anonymous refresh of the articles*), and that does not "
"require a token."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:92
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Anonymous access configuration](../img/users/anonymous_access.1.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid "This allows anyone to update the feeds of the default user’s subscriptions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:95
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For HTTP authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your FreshRSS instance is using HTTP authentication, you’ll need to "
"provide your credentials to the scheduled task."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:100
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** This method is discouraged as your credentials are stored in plain "
"text.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (cron)
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0 * * * * curl -u alice:password123 "
"'https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&maxFeeds=10&ajax=1&user=alice'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid "On some systems, that syntax might also work:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "<https://alice:password123@freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&maxFeeds=10&ajax=1&user=alice>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:109
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For No authentication (None)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your FreshRSS instance uses no authentication (public instance, default "
"user):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "<https://freshrss.example.net/i/?c=feed&a=actualize&maxFeeds=10&ajax=1>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:115
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Feed configuration of “Do not automatically refresh more often than”"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:117
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS does not, by design, supports pull refreshes at frequencies higher "
"than once every 15 minutes. But FreshRSS supports [instant push "
"(WebSub)](websub.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS is part of an RSS ecosystem. A typical reaction that we have seen "
"from several servers is to simply ban by, IP, user-agent, or to remove their "
"RSS feed altogether. Bad user behaviours affect the larger community."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:123
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Default value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:126
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The default value of “Do not automatically refresh more often than” is set "
"in Configuration -> Archiving.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:128
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The lowest global/default purposely cannot be set faster than every 20 "
"minutes, to avoid wasting resources and make sure the RSS ecosystem remains "
"sane."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:129
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Individual feed configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:132
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under the settings for individual feeds, you can go down to 15min."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/refreshing-feeds.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Read more: - [Normal, Global and Reader view](./views.md)  - [Filter the "
"feeds and search](./filtering-articles.md)"
msgstr ""

