#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Share your user queries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A prerequisite is that the FreshRSS API(s) must be enabled in FreshRSS "
"authentication settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"From the configuration page of the user queries, it is possible to share the "
"output of the user queries with external users, in the formats HTML, RSS, "
"and OPML:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Share user query](../img/users/user-query-share.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ℹ️ Note that the sharing as OPML is only available for user queries based "
"on all feeds, a category, or a feed.\n"
"> Sharing by OPML is **not** available for queries based on user labels or "
"favourites or important feeds,\n"
"> to avoid leaking some feed details in an unintended manner.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Additional parameters for shared user queries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid "Some parameters can be manually added to the URL:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid "`f`: Format of output. Can be `html`, `rss` (`atom` is an alias), or `opml`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid "`hours`: Show only the articles newer than this number of hours."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`nb`: Number of articles to return. Limited by `max_posts_per_rss` in the "
"user configuration. Can be used in combination with `offset` for pagination."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`offset`: Skip a number of articles. Used in particular by the HTML view for "
"pagination."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`order`: Show the newest articles at the top with `DESC`, or the oldest "
"articles at the top with `ASC`. By default, will use the sort order defined "
"by the user query."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`search`: Filter the user query results based on search filter. See "
"[Filtering articles](./filtering-articles.md) for more details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:70
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sharing with a master token (deprecated)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Before FreshRSS 1.24, the only option to reshare an RSS output was by using "
"a master token, like "
"`https://freshrss.example.net/?a=rss&user=alice&token=abc123`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This was mostly intended for sharing between systems controlled by the same "
"user, and not for sharing publicly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This method **is not advised anymore** as it is not safe to use the same "
"master token for multiple outputs, especially not when shared with other "
"persons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/user-queries.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Now, sharing RSS outputs via user queries is the recommended approach for "
"all scenarios."
msgstr ""

