msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Website scraping"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"FreshRSS has a built-in [Web "
"scraping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_scraping) engine that generates "
"a feed from websites that have no RSS/Atom feed published."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to add"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to “Subscription Management” where a new feed can be added.  Change the "
"“Type of feed source” to one of: - “HTML + XPath (Web scraping)” - JSON Feed "
"(see [`jsonfeed.org`](https://www.jsonfeed.org/))  - JSON (Dotted paths)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "An additional list of text boxes to configure the Web scraping will show."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For HTML + XPath, [XPath 1.0](https://www.w3.org/TR/xpath-10/) is used as "
"traversing language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get the XPath path"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Firefox: the built-in “inspect” tool may be used to help create a valid "
"XPath expression.  Select the node in the HTML, right click with your mouse "
"and chose “Copy” and “XPath”.  The XPath is stored in your clipboard now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get the JSON dotted path"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Suppose the JSON to which you are subscribing to (or scraping) looks like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"data\": {\n"
"\t\t\"items\": [\n"
"\t\t\t{\n"
"\t\t\t\t\"meta\": {\"title\": \"Some news item\"},\n"
"\t\t\t\t\"content\": \"Content of the news\",\n"
"\t\t\t\t\"links\": [\"https://example.net/1\", \"https://example.org/1\"]\n"
"\t\t\t},\n"
"\t\t\t{\n"
"\t\t\t\t\"meta\": {\"title\": \"Some other news item\"},\n"
"\t\t\t\t\"content\": \"Yet more content\",\n"
"\t\t\t\t\"links\": [\"https://example.net/2\", \"https://example.org/2\"]\n"
"\t\t\t}\n"
"\t\t]\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "The *dot notation* and *bracket notation* (only numeric) are supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Then the items are under `data.items`, and within each item, the title is "
"`meta.title`, and the link would be `links[1]`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is a similar syntax to the JavaScript way to access JSON: "
"`object.object.array[2].property`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Support string concatenation with a syntax like: `meta.title & \" some "
"text\"` using single-quotes or double-quotes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tips & tricks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Timezone of date](https://github.com/FreshRSS/FreshRSS/discussions/5483)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended external manuals"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[XPath Scraping with FreshRSS, by Dan "
"Q](https://danq.me/2022/09/27/freshrss-xpath/) (September 2022)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: en/./users/website-scraping.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A [crowdsourced collection of XPath/scraping "
"settings](https://codeberg.org/gedankenstuecke/freshrss-xpath-scraping-settings-examples) "
"for various websites (incl. News pages). Also has OPML files to easily "
"import settings. (August 2025)"
msgstr ""

